desktop-shell: apps open on the screen they were last on, else the main one

- Each app (by its app id) opens on the screen it was last on: the screen
  of its window when it closed or when a drag of it ended. Kept in
  ~/.config/hexaos/window-screens, one "SCREEN<tab>APP-ID" line each.
- When that screen is not connected, or the app is new, the window opens
  on the main screen: [shell] primary-output=NAME (e.g. HDMI-A-1), chosen
  in Settings > Display or by hexa-setup. Without it, the first screen.
- Dialogs open on their parent window's screen.
- The same goes for windows that open maximized or full screen (Weston
  used the screen with the keyboard focus). Before this, new windows
  opened on the screen under the pointer.

